    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### qTox Version\n\nv1.18.2\n\n### Commit Hash\n\nac1a16ec0bb7ef1f9bbd494a076e661b05937d08\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.20\n\n### Qt Version\n\n6.8.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox\n2. Have a friend\n3. Create a circle with her\n4. Right click the circle\n5. From the context menu select \"Open all in new window\"\n\n\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nAt this point the user is presented an empty qTox window. Details and a screenshot [here](https://github.com/TokTok/qTox/issues/497#issuecomment-2646490430).\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nAll \"things\" should be open in a new window.\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nWindows 10 22H2\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nNo related entries in the log.\n```",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I suppose this might have been meant only for `Multiple windows mode`, where it seems to work alright'ish.\n\nWith `Open each chat in an individual window` the empty window can also be found (in addition to actual chat windows), and I wonder if it's actually the \"circle\" window that is unintentionally opened then.\n",
